course: dictionary
lesson: 211
title: Names and capital letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alexander is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. A name tells you who someone is, not what something is. Alexander is a proper noun, a special word for one particular person, place or thing. «Alexander was late for school again.» Here Alexander is a boy, because a name is the name of a person.
explain: Alexander has short forms you may know: Alex, Al, Xander and Sandy. Many different people share this name, so the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «Alexander Fleming noticed a mould on a dish» means a scientist, while «Alexander the Great» means a famous king from long ago.
explain: When you meet a name you do not know, ask: is this a person, a place or a thing? Look at the capital letter in the middle of a sentence. Then check the other words. They will tell you whether the name belongs to a person, a place or a thing.
fact: Alexander is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Alexander is a boy's first name, and its short forms are Alex, Al, Xander and Sandy.
fact: «Alexander the Great» was a famous king of ancient Macedonia who built a huge empire.
fact: Alexander is also a family name, so you may meet it as a surname.
fact: Many people share the name, so read the sentence to find out which one is meant: «Alexander Graham Bell» made a telephone, and «Alexander Fleming» discovered penicillin.
exercise: «Alexander was late for school again.» What is Alexander in this sentence? | *A boy's name | A kind of food | A colour | A place you can visit
exercise: Which of these is a short form of Alexander? | *Alex | Oliver | Harriet | Sophie
exercise: What was Alexander the Great? | A school teacher | A shop owner in a village | A children's TV presenter | *A famous king of ancient Macedonia
test: Which city is named after Alexander the Great? | Rome | London | Athens | *Alexandria
test: In the sentence «Alexander Graham Bell made a working telephone in 1876», what does Alexander tell you? | A type of mould | *A person's name | A kind of medicine | A place
exam: Jayden reads «Alexander was tired after the match» and asks what Alexander means. What is the best answer? | A common word meaning very tired | *A person's name, written with a capital letter | A place where matches are played | A kind of drink
